The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
timeout = nf_flowtable_time_stamp + flow_offload_get_timeout(flow);
WRITE_ONCE(flow->timeout, timeout);
```
Reason:
The code attempts to update the flow's timeout immediately after a failure without any delay, leading to continuous and rapid retries for hardware offloading. This lack of a frequency limit results in excessive system load due to repeated processing.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (timeout - READ_ONCE(flow->timeout) > HZ)
    WRITE_ONCE(flow->timeout, timeout);
else
    return;
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a condition that checks if the time since the last timeout update exceeds one second (defined by `HZ`). This limits the frequency of timeout updates and hardware offload retries to once per second, thereby reducing unnecessary system load.

